    "id": "nmd",
    "repo": "danielep71/K-IRRBB-NMDs",
    "status": "v0.2.0 – Workbook, data and Excel tests (in progress). The v0.1.0 foundation, closed on 2026-10-09, established source layout, documentation, issue governance, CI and static source checks; v0.2.0 builds the first workbook, data import and Excel test harness. Neither delivers pricing, econometric fitting, a production workbook or certified IRRBB outputs. - Decay model (draft, not validated, milestone v0.3.0): core, public facade IRRBB_Decay, harness cases and example, reviewed on release/v0.3.0 and present here since this branch was levelled with main; built to MODEL_CONTRACTS.md and under review in #36; no Excel evidence is recorded yet. Rate and stable-amount models are not built. - Application profile: an Excel workbook will be the end-user deliverable, assembled from reviewed exported VBA source. - Production calculations live in src/core/ without direct Excel object dependencies; at present the data import's parsing, validation, summaries and fingerprint, and the draft decay calculations. - src/modules/ exposes the documented public facade (the data import and the draft decay model, listed in docs/PUBLIC_API.txt); src/workbook/ contains host glue only. - tests/ holds synthetic fixtures, expected results and the VBA regression harness; evidence from a real Excel run must be separately recorded. - No client data, confidential third-party material, vendor source code or customer-specific models are allowed in Git; the repository and its history are public.",
